{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C header file", "description": "This file defines the interface and data structures for the HTTP Body Content Carrier (BCC) object within an HTTP system. It declares constants for events, function pointer typedefs for various operations (like getting headers, adding headers, predicting body size, notifying events, serializing content), and a class-like structure for the interface with these function pointers. The file is intended for use in an HTTP proxy or server environment to handle body content carrier objects, providing a standardized interface for such objects.", "external_files": ["ansc_ifo_interface.h"], "external_methods": [], "published": ["HTTP_BCC_EVENT_ARRIVED_BODY_PART", "HTTP_BCC_EVENT_ARRIVED_BODY", "HTTP_BCC_EVENT_COMPLETED", "HTTP_BCC_EVENT_OVER_PACKED"], "classes": [{"name": "HTTP_BCC_INTERFACE", "description": "Interface structure for HTTP Body Content Carrier with function pointers for operations such as header management, prediction, notification, and serialization."}], "methods": [{"name": "GetHeaderField", "description": "Retrieves a header field based on header ID."}, {"name": "AddHeaderField", "description": "Adds a header field to the content carrier."}, {"name": "PredictBodySize", "description": "Predicts the size of the body content."}, {"name": "Notify", "description": "Notifies events related to the content carrier, such as arrival of body parts or completion."}, {"name": "Serialize", "description": "Serializes the content carrier's data into a buffer."}], "calls": [], "state": 2, "file_id": 8430, "knowledge_revision": 35086, "git_revision": "7e30f88c4ca54db6e79d70eb5e919c86fb3e3bcf", "ctags": [{"_type": "tag", "name": "ACCESS_HTTP_BCC_INTERFACE", "path": "/home/kavia/workspace/code-generation/kirkstone-7931/rdkb/components/opensource/ccsp/CcspCommonLibrary/source/util_api/http/include/http_ifo_bcc.h", "pattern": "/^#define  ACCESS_HTTP_BCC_INTERFACE(/", "language": "C++", "kind": "macro", "signature